{
  "id": "section-future",
  "moduleId": "verb-tenses",
  "label": "Section 2",
  "title": "Future",
  "summary": "Talk about plans and predictions with -(으)ㄹ 거야, use time words, and compare present, past, and future.",
  "learningObjectives": [
    "Form the future with -ㄹ 거야 after vowels and -을 거야 after consonants",
    "Conjugate ㅏ/ㅗ verbs such as 가다, 오다, and 사다 in the present and past",
    "Use the destination particle 에 and the subject particle 이/가 in context",
    "Compare one sentence across present, past, and future"
  ],
  "newVocabularyIds": ["go", "come", "buy", "meet", "apply", "school", "friend", "coffee", "company", "tomorrow", "yesterday", "today", "that-determiner"],
  "reviewVocabularyIds": ["eat", "study", "korean-language", "rice-meal", "i-me"],
  "grammarConceptIds": ["future-eul-geoya", "present-casual", "past-casual", "destination-e", "subject-i-ga"],
  "estimatedMinutes": 25,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s2-intro",
      "type": "intro",
      "title": "Talking about plans",
      "body": [
        "Use -(으)ㄹ 거야 to talk about many future plans and predictions: 갈 거야 (I will go), 먹을 거야 (I will eat).",
        "After a stem that ends in a vowel, attach -ㄹ 거야. After most stems that end in a consonant, attach -을 거야.",
        "You'll learn verbs for going, coming, buying, meeting, and applying, plus the time words 어제 (yesterday), 오늘 (today), and 내일 (tomorrow). Then you'll compare all three tenses using the same sentence."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-vocab-verbs",
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "title": "New words: five verbs",
      "intro": "Four of these stems end in ㅏ or ㅗ, so they take 아 in the present: the other half of the rule from Section 1.",
      "vocabularyIds": ["go", "come", "buy", "meet", "apply"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-vocab-nouns",
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "title": "New words: people, places, and things",
      "vocabularyIds": ["school", "friend", "coffee", "company", "that-determiner"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-vocab-time",
      "type": "vocabulary",
      "title": "New words: time",
      "intro": "Time words usually come near the start of a sentence and need no particle.",
      "vocabularyIds": ["yesterday", "today", "tomorrow"]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-grammar-a-stems",
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "ㅏ/ㅗ verbs in the present and past",
      "grammarConceptIds": ["present-casual", "past-casual"],
      "body": [
        "In Section 1, every stem took 어 or was a 하다 verb. When the stem's last vowel is ㅏ or ㅗ, the ending is 아 in the present and 았어 in the past.",
        "If the stem ends in ㅏ, the extra 아 simply merges in: 가 + 아 → 가. With ㅗ, the vowels combine: 오 + 아 → 와."
      ],
      "rules": [
        { "pattern": "ㅏ stem + 아 → no change", "explanation": "가다 → 가, 사다 → 사, 만나다 → 만나" },
        { "pattern": "ㅗ stem + 아 → ㅘ", "explanation": "오다 → 와" },
        { "pattern": "past: + ㅆ어", "explanation": "가 → 갔어, 사 → 샀어, 만나 → 만났어, 와 → 왔어" }
      ],
      "forms": [
        { "dictionary": "가다", "vocabularyId": "go", "form": "갔어", "romanization": "gasseo", "english": "went", "parts": [{ "text": "갔어", "kind": "contracted" }], "derivation": "present 가 (ga) · past 가 + 았어 → 갔어" },
        { "dictionary": "오다", "vocabularyId": "come", "form": "왔어", "romanization": "wasseo", "english": "came", "parts": [{ "text": "왔어", "kind": "contracted" }], "derivation": "present 와 (wa) · past 오 + 았어 → 왔어" },
        { "dictionary": "사다", "vocabularyId": "buy", "form": "샀어", "romanization": "sasseo", "english": "bought", "parts": [{ "text": "샀어", "kind": "contracted" }], "derivation": "present 사 (sa) · past 사 + 았어 → 샀어" },
        { "dictionary": "만나다", "vocabularyId": "meet", "form": "만났어", "romanization": "mannasseo", "english": "met", "parts": [{ "text": "만", "kind": "stem" }, { "text": "났어", "kind": "contracted" }], "derivation": "present 만나 (manna) · past 만나 + 았어 → 만났어" },
        { "dictionary": "지원하다", "vocabularyId": "apply", "form": "지원했어", "romanization": "jiwonhaesseo", "english": "applied", "parts": [{ "text": "지원", "kind": "stem" }, { "text": "했어", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "present 지원해 (jiwonhae) · past 하다 → 했어" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-grammar-future",
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Future: -(으)ㄹ 거야",
      "grammarConceptIds": ["future-eul-geoya"],
      "body": [
        "Find the stem, then check its last letter.",
        "Vowel-final stem: add ㄹ directly under the last syllable, then 거야. 가 → 갈 거야.",
        "Consonant-final stem: add 을, then 거야. 먹 → 먹을 거야."
      ],
      "rules": [
        { "pattern": "vowel stem + ㄹ 거야", "explanation": "가 → 갈 거야, 사 → 살 거야, 오 → 올 거야, 지원하 → 지원할 거야" },
        { "pattern": "consonant stem + 을 거야", "explanation": "먹 → 먹을 거야" }
      ],
      "forms": [
        { "dictionary": "가다", "vocabularyId": "go", "form": "갈 거야", "romanization": "gal geoya", "english": "will go", "parts": [{ "text": "갈", "kind": "contracted" }, { "text": "거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "가 + ㄹ → 갈" },
        { "dictionary": "먹다", "vocabularyId": "eat", "form": "먹을 거야", "romanization": "meogeul geoya", "english": "will eat", "parts": [{ "text": "먹", "kind": "stem" }, { "text": "을 거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "consonant stem 먹 + 을 거야" },
        { "dictionary": "사다", "vocabularyId": "buy", "form": "살 거야", "romanization": "sal geoya", "english": "will buy", "parts": [{ "text": "살", "kind": "contracted" }, { "text": "거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "사 + ㄹ → 살" },
        { "dictionary": "만나다", "vocabularyId": "meet", "form": "만날 거야", "romanization": "mannal geoya", "english": "will meet", "parts": [{ "text": "만", "kind": "stem" }, { "text": "날", "kind": "contracted" }, { "text": "거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "만나 + ㄹ → 만날" },
        { "dictionary": "오다", "vocabularyId": "come", "form": "올 거야", "romanization": "ol geoya", "english": "will come", "parts": [{ "text": "올", "kind": "contracted" }, { "text": "거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "오 + ㄹ → 올" },
        { "dictionary": "지원하다", "vocabularyId": "apply", "form": "지원할 거야", "romanization": "jiwonhal geoya", "english": "will apply", "parts": [{ "text": "지원", "kind": "stem" }, { "text": "할", "kind": "contracted" }, { "text": "거야", "kind": "ending" }], "derivation": "하 + ㄹ → 할" }
      ],
      "callout": {
        "title": "Stems that already end in ㄹ",
        "body": [
          "If the stem already ends in ㄹ, just add 거야: 놀다 (to hang out) → 놀 거야 (nol geoya). You'll meet more of these verbs later.",
          "거야 is usually pronounced [꺼야], but it's written and romanized geoya."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-grammar-particles",
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "Where to and who: 에 and 이/가",
      "grammarConceptIds": ["destination-e", "subject-i-ga"],
      "body": [
        "The particle 에 marks a destination or target: the place you go to, or the company you apply to. It has the same form after vowels and consonants.",
        "The subject particle 이/가 marks who does the action. 친구 ends in a vowel, so it takes 가: 친구가 (a friend, as subject)."
      ],
      "rules": [
        { "pattern": "place + 에 가다", "explanation": "학교에 가 = go to school" },
        { "pattern": "target + 에 지원하다", "explanation": "회사에 지원해 = apply to a company" },
        { "pattern": "vowel-final noun + 가", "explanation": "친구가 올 거야 = a friend will come" }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "id": "s2-particle-e-demo",
          "korean": "나는 학교에 갈 거야.",
          "romanization": "Naneun hakgyoe gal geoya.",
          "english": "I will go to school.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "학교에", "romanization": "hakgyoe", "meaning": "to school (destination)", "role": "destination", "marker": "에", "vocabularyId": "school", "grammarConceptId": "destination-e" },
            { "text": "갈 거야", "romanization": "gal geoya", "meaning": "will go", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "go", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-examples-future",
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Future sentences",
      "intro": "Tap a word to see its breakdown. Notice where 내일 (tomorrow) sits.",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "id": "s2-go-future",
          "korean": "나는 내일 학교에 갈 거야.",
          "romanization": "Naneun naeil hakgyoe gal geoya.",
          "english": "I will go to school tomorrow.",
          "literal": "I (topic) · tomorrow · to school · will go",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "내일", "romanization": "naeil", "meaning": "tomorrow", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "tomorrow" },
            { "text": "학교에", "romanization": "hakgyoe", "meaning": "to school (destination)", "role": "destination", "marker": "에", "vocabularyId": "school", "grammarConceptId": "destination-e" },
            { "text": "갈 거야", "romanization": "gal geoya", "meaning": "will go", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "go", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-buy-future",
          "korean": "나는 내일 커피를 살 거야.",
          "romanization": "Naneun naeil keopireul sal geoya.",
          "english": "I will buy coffee tomorrow.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "내일", "romanization": "naeil", "meaning": "tomorrow", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "tomorrow" },
            { "text": "커피를", "romanization": "keopireul", "meaning": "coffee (object)", "role": "object", "marker": "를", "vocabularyId": "coffee", "grammarConceptId": "object-eul-reul" },
            { "text": "살 거야", "romanization": "sal geoya", "meaning": "will buy", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "buy", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-meet-future",
          "korean": "나는 내일 친구를 만날 거야.",
          "romanization": "Naneun naeil chingureul mannal geoya.",
          "english": "I will meet a friend tomorrow.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "내일", "romanization": "naeil", "meaning": "tomorrow", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "tomorrow" },
            { "text": "친구를", "romanization": "chingureul", "meaning": "friend (object)", "role": "object", "marker": "를", "vocabularyId": "friend", "grammarConceptId": "object-eul-reul" },
            { "text": "만날 거야", "romanization": "mannal geoya", "meaning": "will meet", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "meet", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-come-future",
          "korean": "친구가 내일 올 거야.",
          "romanization": "Chinguga naeil ol geoya.",
          "english": "A friend will come tomorrow.",
          "note": "Depending on context, 친구 can mean \"a friend\" or \"my friend.\"",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "친구가", "romanization": "chinguga", "meaning": "friend (subject)", "role": "subject", "marker": "가", "vocabularyId": "friend", "grammarConceptId": "subject-i-ga" },
            { "text": "내일", "romanization": "naeil", "meaning": "tomorrow", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "tomorrow" },
            { "text": "올 거야", "romanization": "ol geoya", "meaning": "will come", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "come", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-apply-future",
          "korean": "나는 그 회사에 지원할 거야.",
          "romanization": "Naneun geu hoesae jiwonhal geoya.",
          "english": "I will apply to that company.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "그", "romanization": "geu", "meaning": "that", "role": "determiner", "vocabularyId": "that-determiner" },
            { "text": "회사에", "romanization": "hoesae", "meaning": "to the company (target)", "role": "destination", "marker": "에", "vocabularyId": "company", "grammarConceptId": "destination-e" },
            { "text": "지원할 거야", "romanization": "jiwonhal geoya", "meaning": "will apply", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "apply", "grammarConceptId": "future-eul-geoya" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-examples-time",
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Time words and tense",
      "intro": "어제 pairs with the past. 오늘 often pairs with the present, which can describe plans for today.",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "id": "s2-meet-past",
          "korean": "나는 어제 친구를 만났어.",
          "romanization": "Naneun eoje chingureul mannasseo.",
          "english": "I met a friend yesterday.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "어제", "romanization": "eoje", "meaning": "yesterday", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "yesterday" },
            { "text": "친구를", "romanization": "chingureul", "meaning": "friend (object)", "role": "object", "marker": "를", "vocabularyId": "friend", "grammarConceptId": "object-eul-reul" },
            { "text": "만났어", "romanization": "mannasseo", "meaning": "met", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "meet", "grammarConceptId": "past-casual" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-come-past",
          "korean": "친구가 어제 왔어.",
          "romanization": "Chinguga eoje wasseo.",
          "english": "A friend came yesterday.",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "친구가", "romanization": "chinguga", "meaning": "friend (subject)", "role": "subject", "marker": "가", "vocabularyId": "friend", "grammarConceptId": "subject-i-ga" },
            { "text": "어제", "romanization": "eoje", "meaning": "yesterday", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "yesterday" },
            { "text": "왔어", "romanization": "wasseo", "meaning": "came", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "come", "grammarConceptId": "past-casual" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "s2-go-today",
          "korean": "나는 오늘 학교에 가.",
          "romanization": "Naneun oneul hakgyoe ga.",
          "english": "I'm going to school today.",
          "note": "The Korean present often covers plans for today or the near future, like English \"I'm going.\"",
          "tokens": [
            { "text": "나는", "romanization": "naneun", "meaning": "I (topic)", "role": "topic", "marker": "는", "vocabularyId": "i-me", "grammarConceptId": "topic-eun-neun" },
            { "text": "오늘", "romanization": "oneul", "meaning": "today", "role": "time", "vocabularyId": "today" },
            { "text": "학교에", "romanization": "hakgyoe", "meaning": "to school (destination)", "role": "destination", "marker": "에", "vocabularyId": "school", "grammarConceptId": "destination-e" },
            { "text": "가", "romanization": "ga", "meaning": "go", "role": "verb", "vocabularyId": "go", "grammarConceptId": "present-casual" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-check-future",
      "type": "quiz",
      "title": "Quick check: future forms",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "q-s2-future-eat",
          "type": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "What is the future form of 먹다 (to eat)?",
          "options": [
            { "id": "a", "text": "먹ㄹ 거야" },
            { "id": "b", "text": "먹을 거야" },
            { "id": "c", "text": "먹었어" }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "b",
          "explanation": "The stem 먹 ends in a consonant (ㄱ), so it takes 을 거야: 먹을 거야 (meogeul geoya). ㄹ cannot attach directly to a syllable that already has a final consonant.",
          "conceptIds": ["future-eul-geoya"],
          "vocabularyIds": ["eat"]
        },
        {
          "id": "q-s2-future-meet",
          "type": "multipleChoice",
          "prompt": "What is the future form of 만나다 (to meet)?",
          "options": [
            { "id": "a", "text": "만날 거야" },
            { "id": "b", "text": "만나을 거야" },
            { "id": "c", "text": "만났어" }
          ],
          "correctOptionId": "a",
          "explanation": "The stem 만나 ends in a vowel, so ㄹ attaches under the last syllable: 만나 → 만날 거야 (mannal geoya). 만났어 is the past.",
          "conceptIds": ["future-eul-geoya"],
          "vocabularyIds": ["meet"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2-compare-three",
      "type": "comparison",
      "title": "Present, past, and future side by side",
      "intro": "The same sentence in three tenses. The Korean present can also describe something happening soon, so 지원해 is closest to \"I'm applying.\"",
      "columns": [
        { "id": "present", "label": "Present", "pattern": "-아/어/해" },
        { "id": "past", "label": "Past", "pattern": "-았어/었어/했어" },
        { "id": "future", "label": "Future", "pattern": "-(으)ㄹ 거야" }
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "school",
          "label": "go to school",
          "vocabularyId": "go",
          "cells": {
            "present": { "id": "s2-cmp-school-present", "korean": "나는 학교에 가.", "romanization": "Naneun hakgyoe ga.", "english": "I go to school.", "highlight": "가" },
            "past": { "id": "s2-cmp-school-past", "korean": "나는 학교에 갔어.", "romanization": "Naneun hakgyoe gasseo.", "english": "I went to school.", "highlight": "갔어" },
            "future": { "id": "s2-cmp-school-future", "korean": "나는 학교에 갈 거야.", "romanization": "Naneun hakgyoe gal geoya.", "english": "I will go to school.", "highlight": "갈 거야" }
